    "Air quality also declined in Mumbai, where readings rose significantly following the holiday period."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Major Indian cities, particularly the national capital, are experiencing a significant decline in air quality following the Deepavali festival. The Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB) has been tasked with clarifying data reporting gaps between official channels and private monitors during the period when fireworks were set off. Reports indicate that the current pollution levels are among the worst observed in the last five years. Contributing factors cited by officials and organizations include seasonal stubble burning in neighboring states, heavy vehicle emissions, and the use of firecrackers. While some groups argue that firecrackers are being unfairly blamed for systemic pollution issues, the Supreme Court has broadened the discourse to include long-term sources of air contamination. Regional authorities in cities like Mumbai have also reported sharp increases in AQI levels, prompting renewed public and policy debates regarding environmental health and the use of green firecrackers.",
